  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_05",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Factors Affecting Flora and Fauna: Land",
    "content": "Land affects natural vegetation directly and indirectly. Fertile level is generally devoted to agriculture. The undulating and rough terrains are areas where grassland and woodlands develop and give shelter to a variety of wildlife.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "estimated_minutes": 4,
      "bloom": "Understand"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_THEO_005",
    "title_hi": "Factors Affecting Flora and Fauna: Land",
    "title_gu": "Factors Affecting Flora and Fauna: Land",
    "body": "Land affects natural vegetation directly and indirectly. Fertile level is generally devoted to agriculture. The undulating and rough terrains are areas where grassland and woodlands develop and give shelter to a variety of wildlife."
  },
  {
    "type": "image",
    "image_url": "assets/images/social_science/class9_social_science_ch10_factors_affecting_flora_and_fauna_soil.png"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_06",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Factors Affecting Flora and Fauna: Soil",
    "content": "Different types of soils provide basis for different types of vegetation. The sandy soils of the desert support cactus and thorny bushes, while wet, marshy, deltaic soils support mangroves.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "estimated_minutes": 4,
      "bloom": "Understand"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_THEO_006",
    "title_hi": "Factors Affecting Flora and Fauna: Soil",
    "title_gu": "Factors Affecting Flora and Fauna: Soil",
    "body": "Different types of soils provide basis for different types of vegetation. The sandy soils of the desert support cactus and thorny bushes, while wet, marshy, deltaic soils support mangroves."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_07",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Step-by-Step: The Role of Climate",
    "content": "Climate involves three main factors: \n1. **Temperature:** The character and extent of vegetation are mainly determined by temperature along with humidity in the air.\n2. **Photoperiod (Sunlight):** The variation in duration of sunlight at different places affects plant growth. Trees grow faster in summer.\n3. **Precipitation:** Areas of heavy rainfall have more dense vegetation as compared to areas of less rainfall.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "estimated_minutes": 6,
      "bloom": "Analyze"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_THEO_007",
    "title_hi": "Step-by-Step: The Role of Climate",
    "title_gu": "Step-by-Step: The Role of Climate",
    "body": "Climate involves three main factors: \n1. **Temperature:** The character and extent of vegetation are mainly determined by temperature along with humidity in the air.\n2. **Photoperiod (Sunlight):** The variation in duration of sunlight at different places affects plant growth. Trees grow faster in summer.\n3. **Precipitation:** Areas of heavy rainfall have more dense vegetation as compared to areas of less rainfall."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_08",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Types of Vegetation in India",
    "content": "The following major types of vegetation may be identified in our country: \n1. Tropical Evergreen Forests\n2. Tropical Deciduous Forests\n3. Tropical Thorn Forests and Scrubs\n4. Montane Forests\n5. Mangrove Forests",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "bloom": "Remember"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_THEO_008",
    "title_hi": "Types of Vegetation in India",
    "title_gu": "Types of Vegetation in India",
    "body": "The following major types of vegetation may be identified in our country: \n1. Tropical Evergreen Forests\n2. Tropical Deciduous Forests\n3. Tropical Thorn Forests and Scrubs\n4. Montane Forests\n5. Mangrove Forests"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_09",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Tropical Evergreen Forests",
    "content": "These forests are restricted to heavy rainfall areas of the Western Ghats and the island groups of Lakshadweep, Andaman and Nicobar. They are at their best in areas having more than 200 cm of rainfall. Trees reach great heights up to 60 meters or even above.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "estimated_minutes": 5,
      "bloom": "Understand"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_THEO_009",
    "title_hi": "Tropical Evergreen Forests",
    "title_gu": "Tropical Evergreen Forests",
    "body": "These forests are restricted to heavy rainfall areas of the Western Ghats and the island groups of Lakshadweep, Andaman and Nicobar. They are at their best in areas having more than 200 cm of rainfall. Trees reach great heights up to 60 meters or even above."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_10",
    "type": "memory_trick",
    "title": "Mnemonic for Evergreen Forest Trees",
    "content": "To remember the important trees of the Tropical Evergreen Forests (Ebony, Mahogany, Rosewood, Rubber, Cinchona), remember the phrase: **E**very **M**onkey **R**eally **R**espects **C**oconuts.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "bloom": "Remember"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_MEMO_010",
    "title_hi": "Mnemonic for Evergreen Forest Trees",
    "title_gu": "Mnemonic for Evergreen Forest Trees",
    "body": "To remember the important trees of the Tropical Evergreen Forests (Ebony, Mahogany, Rosewood, Rubber, Cinchona), remember the phrase: **E**very **M**onkey **R**eally **R**espects **C**oconuts."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_11",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Tropical Deciduous Forests",
    "content": "These are the most widespread forests of India. They are also called the monsoon forests and spread over the region receiving rainfall between 200 cm and 70 cm. Trees of this forest type shed their leaves for about six to eight weeks in dry summer.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "estimated_minutes": 5,
      "bloom": "Understand"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_THEO_011",
    "title_hi": "Tropical Deciduous Forests",
    "title_gu": "Tropical Deciduous Forests",
    "body": "These are the most widespread forests of India. They are also called the monsoon forests and spread over the region receiving rainfall between 200 cm and 70 cm. Trees of this forest type shed their leaves for about six to eight weeks in dry summer."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_12",
    "type": "dictionary_link",
    "title": "Etymology: Deciduous",
    "content": "The word 'Deciduous' comes from the Latin word 'decidere', meaning 'to fall off' (de- 'down' + cadere 'to fall'). It perfectly describes trees that shed their leaves annually.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "bloom": "Remember"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_DICT_012",
    "title_hi": "Etymology: Deciduous",
    "title_gu": "Etymology: Deciduous",
    "body": "The word 'Deciduous' comes from the Latin word 'decidere', meaning 'to fall off' (de- 'down' + cadere 'to fall'). It perfectly describes trees that shed their leaves annually."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_13",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Wildlife of India",
    "content": "Like its flora, India is also rich in its fauna. It has approximately 90,000 animal species. The country has about 2,000 species of birds. They constitute 13% of the world's total. There are 2,546 species of fish, which account for nearly 12% of the world's stock.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "estimated_minutes": 4,
      "bloom": "Understand"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_THEO_013",
    "title_hi": "Wildlife of India",
    "title_gu": "Wildlife of India",
    "body": "Like its flora, India is also rich in its fauna. It has approximately 90,000 animal species. The country has about 2,000 species of birds. They constitute 13% of the world's total. There are 2,546 species of fish, which account for nearly 12% of the world's stock."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_14",
    "type": "real_world_example",
    "title": "The Majestic Elephants",
    "content": "The elephants are the most majestic animals among the mammals. They are found in the hot wet forests of Assam, Karnataka, and Kerala.",
