    "title_gu": "The Majestic Elephants",
    "body": "The elephants are the most majestic animals among the mammals. They are found in the hot wet forests of Assam, Karnataka, and Kerala."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_15",
    "type": "history",
    "title": "Cultural Integration: Wildlife Conservation in Ashoka's Reign",
    "content": "Emperor Ashoka of the Maurya Dynasty was one of the earliest rulers in the world to enact laws for the protection of wildlife. His Rock Edicts clearly prohibited the killing of certain species of animals and birds, reflecting a profound respect for biodiversity rooted in Indian culture.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Advanced",
      "estimated_minutes": 4,
      "bloom": "Analyze"
    },
    "id": "KOBJ_CLAS_SOCI_SCIE_CH10_HIST_015",
    "title_hi": "Cultural Integration: Wildlife Conservation in Ashoka's Reign",
    "title_gu": "Cultural Integration: Wildlife Conservation in Ashoka's Reign",
    "body": "Emperor Ashoka of the Maurya Dynasty was one of the earliest rulers in the world to enact laws for the protection of wildlife. His Rock Edicts clearly prohibited the killing of certain species of animals and birds, reflecting a profound respect for biodiversity rooted in Indian culture."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "BLK_CH10_16",
    "type": "theory",
    "title": "Conservation of Flora and Fauna",
    "content": "Due to excessive exploitation of plants and animal resources by human beings, the ecosystem has been disturbed. To protect the flora and fauna, the government has taken many steps such as setting up National Parks, Wildlife Sanctuaries, and Biosphere Reserves.",
    "universal_block_metadata": {
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "estimated_minutes": 5,
      "bloom": "Apply"
    },
